author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Unknown prefix options with separate and equals-form values retain usage rejection; Recovery help targets validate against current runtime command contracts; Known command-first and nested paths remain correct; Ambiguous values use safe root guidance without a second failed invocation
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: Unknown-prefix-option recovery resolves ownership only from declared core/runtime commands and uses executable root help when unknown arity prevents safe command inference.
expected_result: Never recommend a nonexistent command inferred from an unknown option value; retain targeted declared-command and namespaced recovery.
actual_result: "Seven declared-recovery scenarios and real Node/Bun acceptance passed, including root help, equals values, runtime commands and namespaced aliases; the unsafe-source controller rejects the old inference. Complete source suite: 9686 passed, 2 Windows-only Linux skips and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage."
